2026-06-27 22:34:12,790 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: As a Security & Compliance Officer at Nexus Engineering S.r.l., I can assure that our company has experience with regulatory frameworks such as GDPR, having a Data Protection Officer appointed and being ISO 27001 certified, which covers the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems. Our standard data residency is EU only, and we have a cross-border transfer policy that prohibits transfers outside the EU unless there's an explicit legal basis.

We use anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models to protect personal data. We also implement various data subject rights, including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection. Additionally, we have the capability to perform Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIA), which typically take around 3 weeks to complete.

Regarding technical measures for data protection, our access control standards include multi-factor authentication (MFA) enforcement with methods like TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2). We also design Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) and use Privileged Access Management (PAM) solutions like CyberArk Conjur and HashiCorp Vault.

To ensure the security of our solution, we follow network security architecture patterns such as Zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defence-in-depth. We have Intrusion Detection/Prevention Systems (IDS/IPS) deployed and conduct regular penetration testing, at least annually or after major releases, with partners like Synacktiv and HN Security.

Our AI security controls include protection against prompt injection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, model isolation through inference API, and model update security reviews. We also have a robust audit and logging system in place, logging all queries and ensuring log immutability with SHA-256 hash chaining.

Given these capabilities, I believe we can meet the required security and compliance standards for data hosting within the EU, avoiding transfers outside the EU, and implementing appropriate technical measures for data protection, including encryption. However, it's essential to note that our solution must be designed and implemented according to these principles, ensuring strict GDPR compliance and adherence to other regulatory requirements.
